  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.Shiva Prasad vs State Of Ap on 18 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5062 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/A1 seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.229 of 2019 of Ongole I Town Police Station, Prakasam District, which was registered against him for the offences under Sections 420, 188, 273 of IPC and Sec.58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006'). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 10.08.2019 at 01.30 p.m., when the complainant along with his staff proceeded to Anjali Cool Drinks and Fancy Shop, Court Centre, Ongole, they found a person sitting on a motor bike with a bag containing tobacco products, on enquiry, he revealed that he has been purchasing and selling the tobacco products illegally, the Police seized the same under the cover of mediator's report and registered the same as a case in Crime No.229 of 2019 for the offences stated supra. 3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
